944: - [__cxa_call_unexpected](../../../core/libs/prx/libSceAmpr/Export.cpp) (libSceAmpr) - takes the in-flight exception's unwind header and never returns, as [libcxxabi 18.1.8](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_personality.cpp#L1171-L1211) does. No `std::set_unexpected` is exported and the exception header's unexpected handler is never set, so the handler is always the default one, which calls `std::terminate` ([cxa_default_handlers.cpp](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_default_handlers.cpp#L88-L99)); it therefore forwards to libc's `__cxa_call_terminate`, which begins the catch and runs the current terminate handler. That matches libcxxabi except for which terminate handler runs: there `std::terminate` after `__cxa_begin_catch` ([cxa_exception.cpp L470-L477](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp#L470-L477)) runs the handler saved in the caught exception's header ([cxa_handlers.cpp L72-L93](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_handlers.cpp#L72-L93)), which `__cxa_throw` and `__cxa_init_primary_exception` set to `std::get_terminate()` when the exception is thrown ([cxa_exception.cpp L209-L214](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp#L209-L214), [L279](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/3b5b5c1ec4a3095ab096dd780e84d7ab81f3d7ff/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp#L279)), while here the current global handler runs, as AnyPS5's own `std::terminate` does. The two differ only if `std::set_terminate` was called between the throw and this call. A null header terminates because this emulator's libc `__cxa_begin_catch` terminates on null (libcxxabi does not define that case). Dynamic exception specifications that would let a replaced unexpected handler throw a permitted type are not modelled
